<problem>

<setup>
<selectFromSequence name="a" numToSelect="2" withReplacement="true" from="2" to="10" />

<math name="c" simplify="full">$a[1]-1</math>
<math name="d" simplify="full">$a[2]+1</math>
<math name="solution2" simplify="true">$c/$d</math>
<math name="solutions" unordered="true">0,$solution2</math>
</setup>


Solve for <m>x</m>:
<me>x($a[1]-x)=x+$a[2] x^2</me>

<p>How many solutions are there? <mathInput name="user_num_sol" /></p>

<p>Enter the solutions:</p>

<repeatForSequence length="min($user_num_sol,10)" name="xs">
    <p><m>x =</m> <mathInput /></p>
  </repeatForSequence>

<answer>
  <award>
    <when matchpartial="true">
      <mathList>
        <setup><collect componentType="mathInput" from="$xs" isResponse="true" name="collect_list" /></setup><mathList name="list" extend="$collect_list.value" />
      </mathList>
      =
      <math extend="$solutions" />
    </when>
  </award>

</answer>

  <p>(Don't round your answer, but enter your result as a fraction, if needed.)</p>

<solution>
<p>To solve for <m>x</m>, we move all terms to one side then factor the result.  Subtracting <m>x+$a[2] x^2</m> from both sides of the equation, we obtain:</p>
<md>
  <mrow>x($a[1]-x)\amp =x+$a[2] x^2</mrow>
  <mrow>x($a[1]-x) - x -$a[2] x^2\amp =0</mrow>
  <mrow>x($a[1]-x -1 -$a[2] x)\amp =0</mrow>
  <mrow>x(<math extend="$c" /> -$d x)\amp =0.</mrow>
</md>
<p>Since we have the product of two factors equal to zero, one of the two factors must be zero.</p>

<p>Either <m>x=0</m> or <m><math extend="$c" />-$d x=0</m>.  In the latter case, <m>x=<math extend="$c" />/$d</m>, so the solutions are
<m>x=0</m> and <m>x=$solution2</m>.</p>
</solution>

</problem>